<title>USA: US cash DAP prices steady-higher in light trading.</title>
<headline>US cash DAP prices steady-higher in light trading.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-01-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. cash DAP prices were steady to slightly higher in quiet activity, grain dealers said. Recent DAP exports to China have reduced supplies at the U.S. Gulf, keeping prices firm. Domestic demand should increase in February as dealers boost inventories ahead of spring planting.</p>
<p>DAP prices were narrowly mixed.</p>
<p>				Dlrs/short ton     Chg from Friday</p>
<p>DAP central Fla	   179-180		  up 1.00-unch</p>
<p>DAP central La Gulf     188			up 2.00-unch</p>
<p>Ammonia/La Gulf	   220-225		    unch</p>
